# Qoder Sonus — findings by Inkling 2 Small

- Source: Alibaba / Qoder (`sonus`, Qoder built-in model)
- Date: 2026-11-13 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Qoder Sonus (built-in model)
- **Short description:** Qoder's flagship built-in model, launched 2026-09-10 across the Qoder family (Qoder, Qoder IDE, CLI, JetBrains plugin, QoderWake, Cloud Agents) — positioned for marathon-length autonomous tasks, hard knowledge work and serious coding, with a stated specialty in Computer Use (drives the desktop and pro software). Qoder has not disclosed the underlying model/weights; the forum notes opaque pricing and no published benchmark table.
- **Provider / access:** Qoder (Qoder International / Global) — built into the Qoder model picker; individual and enterprise accounts. Credit multiplier **3.2×** per the launch post (later community notes cite 8× for "SOTA-tier" usage — the docs' exact accounting is unclear). Not available via public API, OpenCode Zen, OpenRouter, or pay-per-token pricing. Bonus: "SOTA Credits" promos bundle Sonus usage (e.g. 8,000 bonus credits on first Pro/Pro+/Ultra monthly subscription, 7-day validity; 2,000-credit October promo).
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-10 (forum announcement, "Sonus is here"). Knowledge cutoff undisclosed.
- **IDs:** `Sonus` (Qoder picker). No API ID or weights published.
- **Context window:** undisclosed (reports of large windows on the platform; unconfirmed).
- **Modalities:** text out; agentic Computer Use (screen control, tool use) per launch post; multimodal input unconfirmed.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** Qoder credits only — 3.2× credit multiplier (launch post); not per-token priced; subscription/bonus-credit structure on first-subscription promos.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed — built-in/proprietary; community suspects routed third-party/undisclosed weights (per Zhihu discussion of Qoder's built-in tiers). Not verified.

### Raw benchmarks found

ZERO verified public benchmark numbers found for `sonus` (the exact Qoder built-in model). Qoder published no benchmark table at launch; a forum thread explicitly requests "transparent, reproducible benchmarks for Sonus and Cantus" (open request, unanswered as of research date). No SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GDPval, or AA-Index entry exists; BenchLM/LLM Stats/BenchmarkList have no rows (checked 2026-11-13 via search). User reports: strong Computer Use demos (video production ~600 credits), slow/queueing at peak times, one complaint of credits being consumed while idle. No evidence is reproducible for this exact ID.

